 ],
 "notes": "Service names ec2messages/ssmmessages/ssm are only in a local in the GT, so the optional SSM endpoints are checked as a gated declared aws_vpc_endpoint whose configuration or gate mentions ssm/ec2messages, and the flag as a false-default variable whose name mentions SSM (the word the prompt uses). The endpoint-to-both-route-tables relation is only checked as a ref to some route table, because route_table_ids are unknown at plan time and a declared list may be a single expression. 'First public subnet' is not checkable; the NAT is only required to sit in a subnet."
}